<Legal
  title="Terms of service · CAN Data Extract"
  heading="Terms of service"
  description={`The terms for using CAN Data Extract, the online app and the desktop app from ${COMPANY}.`}
  updated="2026-10-16"
>
  <h2>The agreement</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are an agreement between you and {COMPANY} (CVR {CVR}),
    {ADDRESS.join(', ')}, for the use of CAN Data Extract: the online app at app.candataextract.com and the
    desktop app. An Enterprise contract takes precedence over these terms where they differ.
  </p>

  <h2>Plans and your data</h2>
  <p>Every plan includes every feature. The plans differ in who can see what you create.</p>
  <h3>Free</h3>
  <p>
    Transforms and traces you create or upload are <strong>public</strong>. Any CAN Data Extract
    user can find, open and copy them. Do not upload traces you are not allowed to publish.
  </p>
  <h3>Pro</h3>
  <p>
    Transforms are <strong>private</strong> to your namespace. Traces are private to your
    namespace, and you grant {COMPANY} the right to use them for <strong>testing and
    validation</strong> of CAN Data Extract. We do not publish them or share them with other customers.
  </p>
  <h3>Enterprise</h3>
  <p>
    Transforms and traces are <strong>private</strong> to your namespace and are not used by
    {COMPANY} for any purpose. Enterprise can be self-hosted, in which case your data stays on
    your servers.
  </p>

  <h2>Working on vehicles</h2>
  <p>
    CAN Data Extract can send diagnostic requests to a vehicle and simulate ECUs on a CAN bus.
    Sending requests to a vehicle can change its state, including clearing fault codes and
    changing sessions. You are responsible for working safely, on vehicles you are allowed to
    work on, and never on a vehicle in motion on a public road.
  </p>

